.TH "tennis" "1" "2026-11-09"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tennis - print stylish CSV tables in your terminal
.PP
https://github.\&com/gurgeous/tennis
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtennis\fR [\fIoptions.\&.\&.\&\fR] <file.\&csv>
.PP
Also supports stdin, json/jsonl, sqlite, etc.\&
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBtennis\fR is a small CLI for printing stylish CSV tables in your terminal.\&
Rows will be truncated to fit and it'\&ll automatically pick nice colors
to match your terminal.\& Works with all \fBCSV\fR variants as well as
\fBJSON/JSONL\fR and \fBSQLite\fR files.\&
.PP
.SH DEMO
.PP
Render a CSV file:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
$ tennis diamonds\&.csv
╭───────┬───────────┬───────┬─────────┬────────┬───────┬───────╮
│ carat │ cut       │ color │ clarity │ depth  │ table │ price │
├───────┼───────────┼───────┼─────────┼────────┼───────┼───────┤
│ 0\&.230 │ Ideal     │ E     │ SI2     │ 61\&.500 │    55 │   326 │
│ 0\&.210 │ Premium   │ E     │ SI1     │ 59\&.800 │    61 │   326 │
│ 0\&.230 │ Good      │ E     │ VS1     │ 56\&.900 │    65 │   327 │
│ 0\&.290 │ Premium   │ I     │ VS2     │ 62\&.400 │    58 │   334 │
│ 0\&.310 │ Good      │ J     │ SI2     │ 63\&.300 │    58 │   335 │
\&.\&.\&.
.fi
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SH POPULAR OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--border\fR <border>
.RS 4
Select the table border style (see below).\& The default is \fBrounded\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--peek\fR
.RS 4
Show the shape, some sample rows, and compact per-column stats.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-n\fR, \fB--row-numbers\fR
.RS 4
Show row numbers.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-p\fR, \fB--pager\fR
.RS 4
Send output through \fB$PAGER\fR or \fBless\fR.\& If \fBLESS\fR is unset, it defaults to
\fBFRX\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-t\fR, \fB--title\fR <string>
.RS 4
Add a title above the table.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--zebra\fR
.RS 4
Turn on zebra stripes.\&
.PP
.PP
.PP
.RE
.SH SORTING & FILTERING
.PP
\fB--filter\fR <string>
.RS 4
Keep rows where any field contains the given text, case-insensitive.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--deselect\fR <headers>
.RS 4
De-select one or more comma-separated headers after any \fB--select\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--head\fR <int>
.RS 4
Show the first \fIN\fR data rows.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-r\fR, \fB--reverse\fR
.RS 4
Reverse row order.\& Helpful when sorting.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--select\fR <headers>
.RS 4
Select, reorder, or repeat one or more comma-separated headers.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--shuffle\fR
.RS 4
Shuffle rows.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--sort\fR <headers>
.RS 4
Sort rows by one or more comma-separated headers.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--table\fR <name>
.RS 4
Select a specific table from a sqlite file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--tail\fR <int>
.RS 4
Show the last \fIN\fR data rows.\&
.PP
.PP
.PP
.RE
.SH TABLE LAYOUT
.PP
\fB-b\fR <headers>
.RS 4
Make these columns Bigger.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-bb\fR <headers>
.RS 4
Make even BIGGER (p90).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-bbb\fR <headers>
.RS 4
Make BIGGEST (full width).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--width\fR <width>
.PP
.RS 4
Set the table width.\& If you specify an integer, it will be used as the
max table width and tennis will truncate to fit if necessary.\& By default,
\fBtennis\fR uses the current terminal width or \fB80\fR if it can'\&t be detected.\&
.PP
Also supports two special values - \fBmin\fR to layout based on header
width, \fBmax\fR to disable truncation entirely.\&
.PP
.PP
.PP
.RE
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--color\fR <color>
.RS 4
Control color output.\& Valid values: \fBon\fR, \fBoff\fR, \fBauto\fR.\& The default is
\fBon\fR.\& Also honors \fBNO_COLOR\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--delimiter\fR <char>
.RS 4
Set the delimiter when reading input.\& Defaults to '\&\fB,\fR'\& naturally.\& It
accepts any char, or \fBtab\fR for tab-delimited input.\& Note that tennis tries
to automatically detect the correct delimiter, so hopefully this is
rarely necessary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--digits\fR <int>
.RS 4
Set the number of digits after the decimal for float columns.\& Valid values
\fB1\fR through \fB6\fR, the default is \fB3\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--scale\fR <headers>
.RS 4
Add a red-to-green color scale to these columns.\& This is similar to
"conditional formatting" in Google Sheets.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--rscale\fR <headers>
.RS 4
Just like --scale, but use green-to-red instead.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--skip\fR <int>
.RS 4
Skip the first N lines of input, e.\&g.\& metadata above the CSV header.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--theme\fR <theme>
.RS 4
Select the color theme.\& Valid values: \fBauto\fR, \fBdark\fR, \fBlight\fR.\& The default
is \fBauto\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--vanilla\fR
.RS 4
Disable type inference and numeric formatting.\&
.PP
.PP
.PP
.PP
.PP
.RE
.SH BORDERS
.PP
Border names are adapted from Nushell table themes, which in turn build on the
\fBtabled\fR crate:
.PP
\fBascii_rounded\fR, \fBbasic\fR, \fBbasic_compact\fR, \fBcompact\fR, \fBcompact_double\fR,
\fBdots\fR, \fBdouble\fR, \fBheavy\fR, \fBlight\fR, \fBmarkdown\fR, \fBnone\fR, \fBpsql\fR,
\fBreinforced\fR, \fBrestructured\fR, \fBrounded\fR, \fBsingle\fR, \fBthin\fR, \fBwith_love\fR
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Render with row numbers and a title:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --row-numbers --title Diamonds diamonds.\&csv # csv
.PP
.RE
Peek at shape, sample rows, and column stats:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --peek diamonds.\&csv
.PP
.RE
Render json, from standard input:
.PP
.RS 4
$ cat diamonds.\&json | tennis
.PP
.RE
Show 20 random rows:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --shuffle --head 20 diamonds.\&csv
.PP
.RE
Select and reorder columns:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --select price,carat,cut diamonds.\&csv
.PP
.RE
Suppress a few columns:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --deselect x,y,z diamonds.\&csv
.PP
.RE
Only show "ideal" diamonds:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --filter ideal diamonds.\&csv
.PP
.RE
Render with a different border:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --border dots diamonds.\&csv
.PP
.RE
Page through a large table:
.PP
.RS 4
$ tennis --pager diamonds.\&csv
.PP
.RE
